<title>USA: Motorola gets Indonesian wireless contract.</title>
<headline>Motorola gets Indonesian wireless contract.</headline>
<dateline>SCHAUMBURG, Ill. 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Motorola Inc said Monday its wireless data group signed an agreement to provide country-wide two-way mobile data communications in Indonesia.</p>
<p>It signed with P.T. Elektrindo Nusantara, Indonesia's first wireless data network operator. The value of the agreement was not disclosed.</p>
<p>Motorola will supply its DataTAC 5000 system, which is scheduled to begin operation during the 1997 first quarter.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
